{"/api/health":{"ok":true,"demo":true,"version":"0.1","ts":"2026-10-23T13:39:05+00:00"},"/api/nle/capabilities":{"verification_notice":"No NLE integration in this build has been executed against a real Premiere Pro or Resolve installation. Every entry is UNVERIFIED until docs/NLE_TEST_LOG.md records a passing real-world test. Do not describe these paths as working to a pilot team.","nle_access_is_user_side":true,"nle_access_note":"Each pilot user/team must obtain and maintain eligible Premiere Pro and Resolve access, including any vendor collaboration entitlement. The platform does not buy, bundle, reimburse or resell those licences, and does not treat them as a platform-service cost.","adapters":[{"key":"premiere.team_projects","nle":"premiere","nle_name":"Adobe Premiere Pro","mode":"vendor_hosted","display_name":"Adobe Team Projects (hosted by Adobe Creative Cloud)","authoritative_state":"team_projects","account_required":true,"user_side_access":"Adobe Creative Cloud subscription (or Teams/Enterprise plan) plus an Adobe ID signed in to the Creative Cloud desktop app, per participating editor.","official_sources":["https://helpx.adobe.com/premiere/desktop/collaborate-with-others/collaborate-using-team-projects/about-team-projects.html","https://helpx.adobe.com/premiere/desktop/collaborate-with-others/collaborate-using-team-projects/collaboration-using-team-projects.html"],"verification_status":"unverified-needs-real-nle-test","known_constraints":["Project metadata, locks and version history are hosted by Adobe (vendor-hosted by definition).","Premiere builds older than 24.6.1 lost Team Projects functionality; version must be current.","Adobe's own help pages conflict on whether Individual CC plans include Team Projects (one page says 'all Creative Cloud subscriptions, including Individual'; secondary sources say Teams/Enterprise only). MUST be verified on the pilot's actual plan before relying on it.","Referenced media must be reachable by every collaborator; originals stay on our host drive."],"unverified_claims":["That Team Projects can consume media through our remote mount at all","That per-sequence locking behaves acceptably over a WAN-mounted path","Publish/version propagation timing"],"originals_stay_local":true,"media_sync_default":"disabled"},{"key":"premiere.productions","nle":"premiere","nle_name":"Adobe Premiere Pro","mode":"private_controlled","display_name":"Premiere Productions on customer-controlled shared storage","authoritative_state":"productions_shared_storage","account_required":true,"user_side_access":"Adobe Premiere Pro licence per editor (Productions is a Premiere feature, not a hosted service) plus compatible customer-controlled shared storage.","official_sources":["https://helpx.adobe.com/premiere/desktop/collaborate-with-others/collaborate-using-productions/about-productions.html"],"verification_status":"unverified-needs-real-nle-test","known_constraints":["Productions is designed around shared storage semantics (NAS/SAN/local shared volume).","Adobe documents that collaborators need access to the same media and project files.","Our peer-to-peer mount is NOT assumed to provide NAS semantics: lock/write/version behaviour on the exact topology must be proven before this mode ships.","A VPN or P2P mount may be slow for media access; Adobe explicitly notes VPN is slow for media."],"unverified_claims":["That project-file locking is safe over a P2P/fuse mount","That concurrent writes cannot corrupt a .prproj on a non-NAS filesystem","Recovery behaviour after an induced offline conflict"],"originals_stay_local":true,"media_sync_default":"disabled"},{"key":"resolve.blackmagic_cloud_project_server","nle":"resolve","nle_name":"DaVinci Resolve","mode":"vendor_hosted","display_name":"Blackmagic Cloud Project Server (hosted project library)","authoritative_state":"blackmagic_cloud_library","account_required":true,"user_side_access":"Blackmagic Cloud ID per collaborator (free account) AND a paid Cloud Project Library hosted by one participant. This fee is USER-SIDE, not a platform cost.","official_sources":["https://www.blackmagicdesign.com/products/davinciresolve/collaboration","https://help.cloud.blackmagicdesign.com/getting-started/free-plan/"],"verification_status":"unverified-needs-real-nle-test","known_constraints":["Official free plan includes only: 2 GB cloud storage, 20 presentations, and ACCESS to libraries others share with you. Creating/hosting a Cloud Project Library is a paid add-on, so vendor-hosted Resolve collaboration is NOT $0 for the host. The host pays, collaborators join free.","Reported fee ~US$5/month per active library (secondary sources; Blackmagic does not publish it on the page we verified) -- treat as unconfirmed and check in the account before promising.","Project library content (bins/timelines/grades) is hosted by Blackmagic in vendor mode.","Media sync and proxy sync must stay DISABLED so originals are not uploaded.","Blackmagic marketing states the free Resolve version includes multi-user collaboration, while some third-party guides claim Studio is required. Must be settled on the pilot's installed version."],"unverified_claims":["Which Resolve edition/version the pilot machines actually need for collaboration","Whether our mount can serve media to a cloud-project Resolve session without media sync"],"originals_stay_local":true,"media_sync_default":"disabled"},{"key":"resolve.private_project_server","nle":"resolve","nle_name":"DaVinci Resolve","mode":"private_controlled","display_name":"DaVinci Resolve Project Server (self-hosted PostgreSQL library)","authoritative_state":"private_project_server","account_required":false,"user_side_access":"DaVinci Resolve install per editor; Blackmagic lists the Project Server app as a free download. A machine must host PostgreSQL and stay online.","official_sources":["https://www.blackmagicdesign.com/products/davinciresolve/collaboration"],"verification_status":"unverified-needs-real-nle-test","known_constraints":["Blackmagic documents the Project Server app as free; it runs on customer hardware.","Historically restricted to the same local network; remote access needs a user-provided VPN or equivalent private path -- which the platform does not pay for.","All-or-nothing library sharing: a shared library has no per-project access control inside it.","Authoritative project state stays on the customer-controlled server (this is the private mode)."],"unverified_claims":["Actual lock behaviour and conflict recovery across our remote mount topology","Whether remote editors can reach a project server outside the LAN without a VPN","Resolve version compatibility across mixed macOS/Windows editors"],"originals_stay_local":true,"media_sync_default":"disabled"}]},"/api/dav/info":{"protocol":"WebDAV, read-only","auth":"HTTP Basic (password = the host bearer token)","transport_security":"none yet — LAN/trusted VPN only until TLS lands","offline_semantics":"503 Service Unavailable, never 404, so NLEs do not treat an offline host as deleted media","depth":"0 and 1 supported; infinity is capped at 1","write_operations":"refused with 405; LOCK/UNLOCK unsupported (501)"},"/api/transfers?limit=1":{"transfers":[{"id":15,"ts":"2026-10-23T06:41:15+00:00","asset_id":"17e2a60a-6d26-466d-a312-c725dab2ce09","session_id":"54a13a92b646","start_byte":0,"end_byte":65535,"bytes":65536,"client":"127.0.0.1","outcome":"ok"}],"total_bytes":131258,"total_requests":15},"/api/selects":{"selects":[{"asset_id":"17e2a60a-6d26-466d-a312-c725dab2ce09","reviewer":"producer","decision":"maybe","note":"Great movement, check the horizon","timecode_ms":null,"created_at":"2026-10-23T06:56:40+00:00","updated_at":"2026-10-23T06:56:40+00:00","name":"DJI_0007.mp4","rel_path":"02_DRONE/DJI_0007.mp4","root_id":"66812071-9602-4eb7-87c5-dd75b2af09dc","media_kind":"video","size_bytes":67109144},{"asset_id":"8b3bfe39-d642-4f12-8b43-a2d2a95656e5","reviewer":"producer","decision":"keep","note":"Hero shot for the open","timeco